menu "Example Configuration"

config EXAMPLE_USE_OPENETH
    bool "Use OpenETH instead of Wi-Fi (QEMU)"
    default n
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32
    select ETH_USE_OPENETH
    help
        Espressif QEMU does not emulate the ESP32 Wi-Fi radio; idf.py qemu
        attaches -nic user,model=open_eth. Enable this to bring up the
        OpenCores Ethernet MAC with DHCP instead of Wi-Fi STA.

        Do not enable on real hardware. QEMU also does not emulate AES/SHA
        hardware well: apply sdkconfig.defaults.qemu (or menuconfig) to
        force software mbedTLS. Set the SimpleOTA token locally; it is not
        stored in the repo.

config EXAMPLE_WIFI_SSID
    string "Wi-Fi SSID"
    default "myssid"
    depends on !EXAMPLE_USE_OPENETH

config EXAMPLE_WIFI_PASSWORD
    string "Wi-Fi password"
    default "mypassword"
    depends on !EXAMPLE_USE_OPENETH

config EXAMPLE_SIMPLEOTA_TOKEN
    string "SimpleOTA project token"
    default "paste-your-project-token"
    help
        Create a project at https://simpleota.com, then copy a project API
        token with the device scope (Project -> API tokens). Keep this in
        local sdkconfig; do not commit a real token.

endmenu
